<asp:Content ContentPlaceHolderID="MainContent" runat="server">

	<img src="20240805_061023.jpg" />

	<p>Since I can't meet Rob for those pictures until Thursday, I decided
to spend the day at a beach. I mean, it <i>is</i> Maui!</p>

	<img src='20240805_061023.jpg' />
	<p>On this part of the island, the sun rises out of sight to the East.
The mountains are north, and show delicate shadows at both sunrise
and sunset. Further north, beyond the mountains, is rainforest. It
rains a lot there, but here in the lee of the mountains' prevailing
winds, not so much (which is why the South Shore of Maui is more
populated than the North Shore.</p>

	<img src='20240805_074334.jpg' />
	<p>Rooftop tents for Jeeps have become a popular choice for Maui
rentals. These tents attach directly to the roof rack system of the
vehicle, providing a convenient and elevated sleeping area. They are
designed to be durable and weather-resistant, often featuring hard
shell or soft shell options. Hard shell tents offer quick setup and
takedown, while soft shell tents provide more space and additional
features like annex rooms. These tents typically include windows and
ventilation to ensure comfort in various weather conditions.</p>
	<p>I would love to have tried one, but with my hip the way it is, climbing the ladder
would've been out of the question. (I had enough trouble crawling into the
back of my SUV.) Maybe next trip, after the hip replacement surgery?</p>

	<img src='20240805_101417.jpg' />
	<p id='Extract'>I called Rob and found he wasn't going to be driving to this side of
the island until Thursday (my last day). So I decided to spend the
day at one of the beach parks I didn't visit that often,
Kanah&amacr;. This beach is near Kahului, and, being on the curve of
coast as it is, you also get spectacular views of the North shores.</p>

	<img src='20240805_101418.jpg' />
	<p>Kanah&amacr; (pronounced kah-nah-HAH) Beach Park is a scenic coastal
park located on the northwestern shore, near the town of Kahului.
Renowned for its expansive sandy beaches and consistent trade winds,
Kanah&amacr; Beach Park is a premier destination for a variety of outdoor
activities and events.</p>

	<img src='20240805_101419.jpg' />
	<p>I think that's that's the town of Waihee-Waiehu. Probably one of the
few spots on the island I haven't already been to.</p>

	<img src='20240805_102314.jpg' />
	<p>Kanah&amacr; Beach Park, located on Maui's north shore, is home to a variety
of native and introduced plant species. Kanah&amacr;'s coastal dunes
and wetlands are adorned with 'aki 'aki (Sporobolus virginicus), a
native grass that thrives in salty environments. Additionally, the
park features lush greenery, including various shrubs and trees that
provide shade and habitat for local wildlife</p>

	<img src='20240805_123415.jpg' />
	<p>There were plenty of cars in the parking lots, but the place is so
big you can easily feel as if you're wandering alone.</p>
<img src='20240805_123613.jpg' />

	<img src='20240805_123757.jpg' />
	<p>As we approach the beach, the first surfers come into view. Maui is
home to every kind of surfing there is; each shore attracts surfers,
windsurfers, kiteboarders, and more in accordance with its waves,
winds, and absence of hazards.</p>

	<img src='20240805_123836.jpg' />
	<p>Kitesurfing, also known as kiteboarding, is a thrilling water sport
that combines aspects of surfing, windsurfing, and paragliding. In
kitesurfing, a large parachute-like kite harnesses the power of the
wind to propel the rider across the water on a small surfboard or
kiteboard. The kite is connected to the rider via a harness, allowing
them to control the kites direction and speed by manipulating a
control bar.</p><p>To be honest, this isn't really anything I'd want
to <i>do</i>. But it's a lot of fun to watch!</p>

	<img src='20240805_123842.jpg' />
	<p>And if kiteboarding is too advanced for you, there's still
windsurfing! This is an exhilarating water sport that combines
elements of both sailing and surfing. It involves riding on a board,
known as a sailboard, which is powered by the wind through a sail
attached to a movable mast. The rider stands on the board and uses
the sail to catch the wind, propelling themselves across the water.
By adjusting the sails angle and position, the windsurfer can control
their speed and direction.</p>
<img src='20240805_123925.jpg' />

	<img src='20240805_124108.jpg' />
	<p>I made friends with one of the surfers, a guy named Gary. He was born
on Maui and surfs every day. When he needs money, he asks visitors if
they want surf lessons.</p><p>He's never short of money.</p>
<video autoplay='autoplay' loop='loop'>
	<source src='20240805_124605.mp4' />
</video>

	<img src='20240805_151702.jpg' />
	<p>Part of the fun of being 73 is having to go to the bathroom, like,
every fifteen minutes. So on the way back to the campground, I pulled
into Maui Lani Regional Park, where I used to let the dogs run, and
where I knew there was a decent restroom. That community on the lower
slope is Wailuku.</p>

	<img src='20240805_204331.jpg' />
	<p>Anyway, I made it back to Camp Oluwalu well before dark. And I was
still jetlagged, so I again went to sleep early. But I awoke around 1
AM (another perk of being old) to be reminded how amazing the night
sky is in a Dark Skies-designated area.</p><p>DarkSky International
is an organization which works to protect night skies for present and
future generations through outreach, advocacy, and conservation. They
certify communities, parks, and protected areas around the world as
International Dark Sky Places, ensuring these locations maintain
responsible lighting policies and public education efforts.</p>

<p>So, back to bed&hellip;I've decided tomorrow to drive to the 
	top of Mount Haleakala, a trip I haven't made since before
	the pandemic.</p>
	
